WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.640
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:12.800
Today we are going to have an AI write a story&nbsp;
for us, and even do our coding exam materials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.240
And the coolest thing is that both&nbsp;
of these will be done by the same AI.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:28.080
How? Well, OpenAI’s GPT-3 technique is capable of&nbsp;
all kinds of wizardry as long as it involves text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:35.360
processing. For instance, finishing our sentences,&nbsp;
or creating plots, spreadsheets, mathematical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:43.040
formulae, and many other things. While their&nbsp;
Dall-E 2 AI is capable of generating incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:51.280
quality images from our written descriptions.&nbsp;
Even if they are too specific. Way too specific.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.080
Now, today, we are going to play&nbsp;
with GPT-3, the text AI that just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:04.480
gained an amazing new capability. And&nbsp;
that is, editing and inserting text.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:11.040
And if you think that this doesn’t sound&nbsp;
much, well, check out these examples.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:19.600
Let’s start a story. Today’s the big day! It says.&nbsp;
Now, the AI sees that the name of the section&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:26.160
is high school graduation, and it infers, quite&nbsp;
intelligently that this might be a message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:33.280
from a school to their graduating students. So&nbsp;
far so good, but this was possible before too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.720
So what’s new here? Well, hold on to&nbsp;
your papers, and now, let’s do…this!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:49.200
Oh yes. Change the story. Now, we don’t know why&nbsp;
is this the big day, but we know that the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:58.320
section will be about moving to San Francisco,&nbsp;
and…oh my! Look at that! It understood the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:06.080
trick, and rewrote the story accordingly. But,&nbsp;
you know what? If we wish to move to Istanbul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:14.400
instead - not a problem. The AI gets that one&nbsp;
too. Or, if we have grown tired of the city life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.080
we can move to a farm too, and have&nbsp;
the AI write out story for that.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:29.600
Okay, that was fantastic, but when it comes to&nbsp;
completion, I have an idea. Listen. How about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:36.320
pretending that we know how to make hot&nbsp;
chocolate. Fill in the last step, which is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:43.920
you know, not a great contribution, and let the AI&nbsp;
do the rest of the dirty work. And can it do that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:51.920
Wow, it knows exactly that this is recipe,&nbsp;
and it knows how to fill that in correctly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:57.360
I love it. The put hot chocolate&nbsp;
part is a bit of a copout,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:04.160
but you know what, I’ll take it. From the&nbsp;
recipe, it sounds like a good one. Cheers!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:14.960
Now, let’s write a poem about GPT-3. There we go!&nbsp;
It rhymes too, checkmark. And now, let’s ask the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:24.720
AI to rephrase it in its own voice. And…yes! It is&nbsp;
able to do that, while carefully keeping the rhyme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:33.200
intact. And when we ask it to sign it, look.&nbsp;
We get a letter to humanity. How cool is that?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.400
Now, onwards to coding. And this is&nbsp;
where things get really interesting.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.800
Here is a piece of code for computing&nbsp;
Fibonacci numbers. Now, translate it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:52.880
into a different programming language. Wow, that&nbsp;
was quick. Now, rewrite it to do the same thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:04:01.040
but the code has to fit one line. And here comes&nbsp;
my favorite: improve the runtime complexity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:09.840
of the code. In other words, make it more&nbsp;
efficient. And there we go. Now, clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:17.760
you see that this is a simple assignment, yes.&nbsp;
But. Make no mistake, these are fantastic signs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:24.960
that an AI is now capable of doing meaningful&nbsp;
programming work. And if you have a friend who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:31.200
conducted coding interviews, show it to them. I&nbsp;
reckon they will say that they have met plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.960
of human applicants who would do worse than this.&nbsp;
If you have your own stories, you know what to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.000
Of course, leave them in the comments&nbsp;
section, I'd love to hear them.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.720
And, if you have been holding&nbsp;
on to your papers so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:53.440
now, squeeze that paper because here comes the&nbsp;
best part. We will fuse the two previous examples&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:05:01.120
together. What does that mean? Well, we will use&nbsp;
the hot chocolate playbook and apply it to coding.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:08.560
Let’s construct the start and the end of&nbsp;
the code, and hand it away to the AI. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:16.160
yes, once again, it has a good idea as to&nbsp;
what we are trying to do, it carefully looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:22.400
at our variable names and fills in the key&nbsp;
part of the code in a way that no one will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:27.840
be able to tell that we haven’t been doing&nbsp;
our work properly. What a time to be alive!

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:36.560
So, an AI that can write a story for us, even in a&nbsp;
way that we only have to give it the scaffoldings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:44.320
in the story, and it fills in the rest. I&nbsp;
love it. So cool! And it can help us with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:51.840
our coding problems, and even help us save a ton&nbsp;
of time massaging our data into different forms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.360
What an incredible step forward in&nbsp;
democratizing these amazing AIs.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:03.600
So, what would you use this for? What do you&nbsp;
expect to happen a couple more papers down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.680
line? Please let me know in the comments&nbsp;
below. I’d love to hear your thoughts.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.320
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

